& [Objective]
  + promote the smallest effect-free semantic nucleus observed in live cantor_scribe into a separately governed reusable Cantor kernel component
  + preserve exact source attribution while adapting the nucleus to the current published Cantor lineage and instance contract

& [Requirements]
  + [CSSK-001] preserve dictated source and exact selected live-source byte identities before derived formation or Rust implementation
  + [CSSK-002] use published bookend 4209d44228399c8aa01b2ccb98806777c65826b8 as predecessor
  + [CSSK-003] do not modify delete stage normalize or otherwise disturb the live C checkout
  + [CSSK-004] implement a new safe-Rust workspace crate named cantor_sop_semantics rather than copying or admitting cantor_scribe wholesale
  + [CSSK-005] retain normalized document semantic forms including dependencies subjects perspectives data fields roles relations expressions views and source spans
  + [CSSK-006] retain domain-separated deterministic SHA256 generation and document-manifest construction
  + [CSSK-007] retain bounded validation for document identity dependency identity duplicate semantic identity source spans roles relations expressions and views
  + [CSSK-008] retain three-valued expression evaluation with explicit unknown propagation
  + [CSSK-009] retain exact source parsing diagnostics partial-document recovery and byte spans for the bounded SOP grammar
  + [CSSK-010] refuse unknown supplied machine fields and duplicate members for every semantic set
  + [CSSK-011] adapt faults so the promoted crate contains no ambient I/O or SQLite conversion
  + [CSSK-012] statically exclude filesystem process environment database async transport LSP MCP network provider CLI unsafe and live-effect surfaces
  + [CSSK-013] expose a pure semantic analysis entry point and deterministic machine form suitable for later kernel composition
  + [CSSK-014] bind the promoted component to kernel capability kernel.sop.semantic-analyze without granting execution provider operator update publication or mutation authority
  + [CSSK-015] test constructive documents normalization generation validation expressions source analysis partial recovery and deterministic replay
  + [CSSK-016] test malformed source invalid spans duplicate identities duplicate supplied set members unknown fields expression limits unsupported operators and digest tampering
  + [CSSK-017] independently verify the six selected live-source files still match their recorded path byte count and SHA256
  + [CSSK-018] verify focused debug overflow-checked release warnings-denied Clippy format exact workspace and recursive evidence gates
  + [CSSK-019] publish only owned source formation implementation tests evidence and intentional transitive manifests
  + [CSSK-020] retain SQLite storage project I/O query revision draft search LSP MCP Tokio transports provider and live execution as unresolved separately governed candidates

& [Acceptance]
  + [CSSK-A01] source justification plan solution matrix phase lock and satisfaction signature cross-bind exactly
  + [CSSK-A02] selected-source custody independently replays from the unchanged live checkout
  + [CSSK-A03] focused constructive adversarial static-absence and fresh-process semantic analysis gates pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [CSSK-A04] exact workspace Clippy format and recursive evidence pass before completion publication
  + [CSSK-A05] integration evidence promotes only the bounded capability while the whole cantor_scribe candidate remains held

& [NonAuthority]
  + semantic analysis is pure structural computation and does not authorize filesystem access execution model inference provider contact installation update remote mutation publication or any external effect
  + source custody and passing tests do not admit the remainder of cantor_scribe or the live SOP Eclipse checkout
